# DIAGNOSTICS

A command `/dev/reboot` doesn't know, or one the machine refuses (`poweroff` on an amd64 machine without `\_S5`, a warm boot the kernel refuses), fails its write: `echo: write error`.
`warmboot` with too few arguments prints its usage and exits `usage`; a file it can't copy, `copy`; a warm boot refused, `refused`.

# BUGS

`warmboot` runs on amd64 and arm64, not yet rv64.
On arm64 the GIC's LPIs are turned off for the next kernel; a GIC whose LPIs, once on, can't be turned off (the architecture allows it) would go on writing the old tables.
Through a cpu(8) session the images cross the link at about 120 MB/s under KVM, and much slower without, so a 100 MB bootfs takes under a second to copy, or many seconds under TCG.
The new boot's command line replaces this one's whole; there is no way to add one option to it.
